diff --git a/docs/GUIDE.md b/docs/GUIDE.md
index fc409ab..3a5c24f 100644
--- a/docs/GUIDE.md
+++ b/docs/GUIDE.md
@@ -1293,6 +1293,21 @@ make install APP=~/GameDevWorkstationUpdates/<version>/GameDevWorkstation.app
 
 `make install` with no `APP` installs `dist/GameDevWorkstation.app` from `make app`.
 
+**Automatic install.** With `[updates] auto_install = true` (the default), a pending update
+installs by itself once no session is running. Each version is tried once only, so a failed
+install never loops. **Install & restart** still works by hand.
+
+**GitHub Releases.** When `main` has a `VERSION` that has no release yet, the release workflow
+(`.github/workflows/release.yml`) builds the macOS app (`GameDevWorkstation-<version>-macos-arm64.zip`
+and `.dmg`) and the Windows installer (`GameDevWorkstation-<version>-x64-setup.exe`). It publishes
+them as release `v<version>`. These builds carry the `github` update channel: every
+`[updates] github_interval_s` (default 6 hours) they check the latest release, download the
+asset for their platform into the updates folder (same layout as `make release`) and the
+folder updater takes it from there. Local builds (`make app`, `make release`) never call GitHub.
+
+On Windows a release is an installer. To install it, a PowerShell helper stops the app, runs the
+installer silently (`/S`) and starts the app again. Rollback isn't available there.
+
